---
import { MapIcon } from "lucide-solid";
---

<footer class="mt-20 bg-ink">
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-khaki-300">
      Tilik is informational only. It pulls from open data that can be incomplete,
      out of date, or wrong for your exact plot. It is not a survey, not legal or
      financial advice, and not a guarantee about any property. Before you sign
      anything, get a licensed surveyor and check local government records.
    </p>

    <div
      class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-khaki-700 pt-5 text-sm text-khaki-300"
    >
    <img
      src="/tilik-light.png"
      alt=""
      width="40"
      height="40"
      class="h-10 w-auto shrink-0"
    />
      <span class="text-khaki-600">·</span>
      <a href="/guideline" class="transition-colors hover:text-clay-300">How to use it</a>
      <span class="text-khaki-600">·</span>
      <span>Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors</span>
      <span class="text-khaki-600">·</span>
      <a href="/api/health" class="transition-colors hover:text-clay-300">API status</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
